From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: DIAGNOSTIC: Add Oculus Quest 2 watchdog-timing
 boot beacon

Debug aid for kernels that hang early after the kexec handoff on the
Oculus Quest 2, which has no serial console. Not for upstream.

Five early boot checkpoints (primary_entry, after paging_init(), before
rest_init(), after smp_init(), before the device initcalls) each wait
21 s and re-arm the APSS watchdog with a 31.5 s bite, so the time from
the handoff to the watchdog reset shows the last checkpoint reached.
This adds about 84 s to every boot and hard-codes an SM8250 address.

Signed-off-by: mac <xmachd@gmail.com>
